---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { checkerUrl, sitePath } from '../../lib/urls';
---

<Page
  article
  title="Instagram export troubleshooting: files and usable results"
  description="Resolve missing directions, split JSON and HTML exports, ZIP selection, ambiguous files and known upload limitations."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">GUIDE · LOCAL FILES</p><h1>
    Get a useful comparison from your files.
  </h1>
  <p class="lede">
    MutualLens compares your uploaded followers and following immediately. An
    account label, date and completeness checkbox are not required.
  </p>
  <h2>A whole direction is missing</h2><p>
    Include both followers and following. A missing file is different from a
    recognized list containing zero records. The checker requests the missing
    direction instead of silently treating it as empty.
  </p>
  <h2>A file needs a direction</h2><p>
    Some loose files contain valid relationship records without identifying
    whether they are followers or following. Use the file assignment controls
    and choose from the original export context. Never infer direction from
    which list has more accounts.
  </p>
  <h2>Split files and ZIP downloads</h2><p>
    Select all relevant parts together, including multiple ZIP downloads from
    the same export. Nested relationship folders are recognized. The importer
    selects relevant relationship entries without expanding unrelated photos,
    videos or messages.
  </p>
  <h2>Known omissions still produce useful results</h2><p>
    If both lists are usable but numbered parts or individual records are
    missing, the report shows qualified differences such as “Not found in
    supplied followers.” It explains skipped or isolated records and includes
    these limitations in downloads. This is a comparison of usable supplied
    records, not a confirmed current relationship claim.
  </p>
  <h2>JSON, HTML and saved MutualLens datasets</h2><p>
    Supported relationship JSON and HTML exports can be selected directly or
    inside ZIP archives. HTML is read as inert data: uploaded scripts, images
    and links are not executed or fetched. MutualLens dataset JSON can be
    reopened after schema validation. Renaming an unrelated file does not make
    it a relationship list.
  </p>
  <h2>Corrupt files or resource limits</h2><p>
    Keep the original files and follow the specific error. Archive metadata,
    relevant decompression and parsed relationship data have security budgets. A
    rejected corrupt or oversized relevant entry needs a fresh export or the
    smallest useful selection of followers and following parts; it is not an
    account-count cutoff.
  </p>
  <h2>Optional history details</h2><p>
    Basic comparison does not need your username or source date. Compatible
    historical comparison needs a matching known account label or stable ID and
    known, ordered collection dates. Two unlabeled snapshots are not assumed to
    describe the same account.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href={checkerUrl('import')}>Open upload mode</a> or <a
      href={sitePath('/guides/download-instagram-followers/')}
      >prepare your export</a
    >.
  </p>
  <p><a href={sitePath('/guides/')}>Browse all MutualLens guides</a>.</p>
</Page>
